Subject: [M150] Ensure gradient data pointers remain safe to use
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Original change's description:
> Ensure gradient data pointers remain safe to use
>
> This patch avoids holding a reference into `gradient_map_` across
> `BuildGradientData()`, which can modify the gradient map. Instead,
> look up the cached entry first and insert the newly built
> `GradientData` into `gradient_map_` afterward.
>
> Fixed: 570675085
> Change-Id: I9c6acde97024951a34b7a39bb8b8e146e07911e9
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8527725
> Auto-Submit: Philip Rogers <pdr@chromium.org>
> Reviewed-by: Fredrik Söderquist <fs@opera.com>
> Commit-Queue: Fredrik Söderquist <fs@opera.com>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714266}

(cherry picked from commit beee6bb7ce5bcda1cf8f825c217d3f49e6364635)

